-- the stat buffer read as a region of 256 bytes: its two time fields are the Int64 cells at byte 88 and
-- byte 96, named with the proofs that those cells fit inside 256 bytes, so neither read can be outside
-- the buffer and the proof is the type's and not a reader's (2026-11-18)
h-stat-time : Word → RM 256 Word
h-stat-time r = λ b → (b , if weq r #0
  then wadd (wmul (wofi64 (load64 256 b 88 (160 , λ i → 256))) #1000000000) (wofi64 (load64 256 b 96 (152 , λ i → 256)))
  else #0)
